## Requirements

### Functional Requirements

- **FR-001**: Warehouse employees can create a supplier order.
- **FR-002**: A supplier order includes the supplier or manufacturer.
- **FR-003**: A supplier order includes the customer number.
- **FR-004**: A supplier order includes the order date.
- **FR-005**: A supplier order includes a P.O. number.
- **FR-006**: Products can be added to a supplier order.
- **FR-007**: Each product includes a SKU, description, number of cases, price, and total.
- **FR-008**: Warehouse employees can create shipment records.
- **FR-009**: shipments includes where the products are being shipped to.
- **FR-010**: shipments includes where the products are being shipped from.
- **FR-011**: shipments includes the customer number.
- **FR-012**: shipments includes the date it was shipped.
- **FR-013**: shipments includes the P.O. number.
- **FR-014**: shipments includes the driver.
- **FR-015**: Products on a shipment include a SKU, description, quantity, price, and total.
- **FR-016**: shipments can have a delivery date once it has been delivered.
- **FR-017**: shipments can record who received it.
- **FR-018**: suppliers order can record who authorized the order.
- **FR-019**: The order date is saved with the supplier order.
- **FR-020**: Required information must be entered before an order or shipment can be saved.

---

## Assumptions

- Warehouse employees will use this feature to keep track of supplier orders and shipments.
- Each supplier order is connected to a supplier or manufacturer.
- All supplier orders are associated with a particular supplier or manufacturer
- A product can be identified by its SKU
- The P.O. number can be used to associate an order with a shipment
- The fields on the Supplier Order Form and Bill of Lading will be represented in this feature's data models
- User authentication and permissions are outside the scope of this feature
- Inventory management and warehouse location tracking are outside the scope of this feature
- Payment handling and processing are outside the scope of this feature
- Shipping arrangements and delivery scheduling are outside the scope of this feature

---

## Edge Cases

- **Missing required information:** The user is told what information is missing and cannot save the record until it is entered.
- **Duplicate P.O. number:** The system warns the user if the P.O. number is already being used.
- **Invalid quantity:** A quantity must be greater than zero.
- **Invalid price:** The price must be entered as a valid monetary value.
- **Missing SKU:** A product cannot be saved without a required SKU.
- **Missing destination:** A shipment cannot be saved without a shipping destination.
- **Missing driver:** The system identifies the missing driver when a driver is required.
- **Shipment has not arrived:** Delivery and receiving information can be left blank until the shipment arrives.
- **Missing P.O. number:** The system identifies the missing P.O. number when it is needed to connect the shipment to an order.

